---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const updated = '2026-05-15';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Legal & takedown"
  description="Trademark policy, removal requests, and how opentier handles legal questions about listed services."
  canonical="https://opentier.dev/legal"
>
  <article class="legal-page container-narrow">
    <p class="rom-eyebrow">
      <span class="rom">§</span> LEGAL
      <span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
      Updated <time datetime={updated}>{updated}</time>
    </p>

    <h1>Legal &amp; takedown</h1>

    <p class="lede">
      opentier is an independent, open-source catalog. We have no commercial relationship with any
      service we list, and we don't accept paid placement. This page covers trademarks, takedown
      requests, and the limits of our editorial responsibility.
    </p>

    <section class="block">
      <h2><span class="rom">i.</span> Trademarks</h2>
      <p>
        Every service name, logo, and brand color shown on this site is the property of its
        respective owner. We use them under fair-use principles for editorial commentary,
        comparison, and identification only. <strong
          >opentier is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by</strong
        > any service listed in the catalog.
      </p>
      <p>
        Logos are sourced from <a href="https://simpleicons.org" rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >simpleicons.org</a
        >
        (CC0), <a href="https://lobehub.com/icons" rel="noopener noreferrer">lobe-icons</a> (MIT), and
        other open-license libraries. Where we couldn't source a free-license version, we use a brand-colored
        placeholder. The full provenance is documented in
        <code>docs/logo-coverage.md</code> in the repository.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2><span class="rom">ii.</span> Takedown requests</h2>
      <p>
        If you represent a service we list and want us to remove or correct its entry, email
        <a href="mailto:removals@opentier.dev">removals@opentier.dev</a>. Please include:
      </p>
      <ul class="legal-list">
        <li>The service name + URL of the entry on opentier</li>
        <li>What you'd like removed or corrected (logo, name, free-tier description, etc.)</li>
        <li>Confirmation that you're authorized to make the request on the service's behalf</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We aim to respond within <strong>48 hours</strong> on business days. Most requests resolve within
        a week. If a service has been wholly retired or its free tier shut down, we move the entry to
        "Services we don't include" rather than delete the record outright — the history helps future
        contributors avoid re-listing.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2><span class="rom">iii.</span> Pricing & free-tier accuracy</h2>
      <p>
        Every entry has a <code>date_verified</code> field showing when we last checked the service's
        pricing page against what we claim. Pricing pages change; we re-verify monthly and accept community
        correction reports via
        <a
          href="https://github.com/Pratiyush/opentier/issues/new?template=02-pricing-change.yml"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub issues</a
        >.
      </p>
      <p>
        We don't warrant accuracy beyond best-effort verification. Always confirm the service's live
        pricing before relying on a specific quota.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2><span class="rom">iv.</span> Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        opentier runs as a static site with no cookies, no trackers, and no analytics that identify
        you. Outbound links go directly to the listed service's own URL without affiliate parameters
        or referral tags.
      </p>
      <p>
        If we ever add opt-in analytics (Cloudflare Web Analytics, no PII, no cookies — currently
        deferred), it will be documented here and on
        <a href="/methodology">/methodology</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2><span class="rom">v.</span> Licensing</h2>
      <p>
        The opentier source code is MIT-licensed. The catalog data (service YAMLs under
        <code>src/content/services/</code>) is published under
        <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/" rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >CC0 1.0</a
        > — public domain, free to use without attribution. We'd appreciate a link back, but it isn't
        required.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2><span class="rom">vi.</span> Contact</h2>
      <ul class="legal-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Takedowns / corrections:</strong>
          <a href="mailto:removals@opentier.dev">removals@opentier.dev</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Editorial questions:</strong>
          file a
          <a
            href="https://github.com/Pratiyush/opentier/issues/new/choose"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub issue</a
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Security disclosures:</strong>
          email the maintainer at <a href="mailto:pratiyush1@gmail.com">pratiyush1@gmail.com</a> with
          subject prefix <code>[security]</code>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>

  <style>
    .legal-page {
      padding-top: var(--space-xl);
      padding-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
    }
    .rom-eyebrow {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.16em;
      color: var(--color-ink-faint);
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
      display: flex;
      align-items: baseline;
      gap: 0.5em;
    }
    .rom {
      color: var(--color-coral);
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-style: italic;
      font-size: 1.1em;
    }
    .dot {
      color: var(--color-rule);
    }
    .legal-page h1 {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.8rem);
      font-weight: 400;
      font-style: italic;
      letter-spacing: -0.015em;
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
      line-height: 1.1;
    }
    .lede {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: 1.15rem;
      font-weight: 350;
      color: var(--color-ink);
      line-height: 1.55;
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-xl);
      max-width: 58ch;
    }
    .block {
      padding: var(--space-lg) 0;
      border-top: var(--border-rule);
      max-width: 65ch;
    }
    .block h2 {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: 1.4rem;
      font-weight: 500;
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
      display: flex;
      align-items: baseline;
      gap: 0.5em;
    }
    .block p {
      line-height: 1.65;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
      color: var(--color-ink);
    }
    .block a {
      color: var(--color-ink);
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-decoration-color: var(--color-coral);
    }
    .legal-list {
      list-style: none;
      padding: 0;
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
    }
    .legal-list li {
      padding-left: 1.4em;
      text-indent: -1.4em;
      line-height: 1.55;
      margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
    }
    .legal-list li::before {
      content: '— ';
      color: var(--color-coral);
    }
    code {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.88em;
      padding: 0.1rem 0.3rem;
      background: var(--color-paper-warm);
      border-radius: 3px;
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
